## 6. What Remains Open

This theorem does not:

- print an infinite digit list or a global number-field formula;
- give a universal syzygy valid on every component of the coefficient
  scheme;
- select one of the 123 coefficient-kernel directions physically;
- prove that the previously frozen number-field member `C_Q` is the same
  graph-Prym member;
- select a smooth characteristic-zero member and evaluate `beta_C` on that
  same member;
- construct the twisted visible bundle, HYM connection, or
  Hull-Strominger endpoint.

`UST.G3AJ` subsequently proves that the selected residue coefficient ball
contains a smooth finite-flat rank-three graph-Prym member. The remaining
nonduplicative target is the explicit analytic selection problem:

```text
emit/select a member of the formal graph-Prym residue ball
  -> calculate beta_C on that member
  -> promote the algebraic Prym line to the twisted visible V3.
```

